{
 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "Draw two overlapping circles inside a rectangle",
   "Fill in the intersection first",
   "Subtract the intersection from each individual total",
   "Put what's left in the 'neither' region",
   "For conditional probability: P(A|B) = n(A∩B) / n(B)"
  ],
  "title": "Venn Diagrams & Conditional Probability",
  "content": "<p><strong>Venn diagrams</strong> show overlapping sets. \\(P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)\\). The region outside both circles = \\(P(\\text{neither})\\).</p><p><strong>Conditional probability:</strong> \\(P(A | B) = \\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}\\). Read as 'probability of A given B has occurred'.</p><p>Fill in a Venn diagram from the <strong>intersection first</strong>, then work outward. Total of all regions = 1 (or the total number of items).</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>30 students: 18 like football, 12 like tennis, 6 like both.</strong></p><p>Football only: 12, Both: 6, Tennis only: 6, Neither: 6. P(football | tennis) = 6/12 = 1/2.</p>"
 },
